can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":2886,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/organoid-dependency-data/4671/3","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":7111,"name":"","username":"MarkoFlow","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.depmap.org/markoflow/{size}/1687_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-19T13:12:11.518Z","cooked":"\u003caside class=\"quote no-group quote-modified\" data-username=\"danieljgorski\" data-post=\"3\" data-topic=\"4671\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"title\"\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"quote-controls\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cimg alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/d/3be4f8/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"\u003e danieljgorski:\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJust wondering, are there plans to also release the count level data for these models? From what I see in the \u003ca href=\"https://hobistudio.si/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://hobistudio.si/\u003c/a\u003e “NextGen Model Manuscript 2026 Files” only log2(TPM+1) \u003ca href=\"https://eldfall-chronicles.com/sl/blogs/blog/understanding-board-game-mechanics-through-eldfall-chronicles\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003emehanike namiznih iger\u003c/a\u003e values are available in the “next_gen_expression.csv” file.\u003cbr\u003e\nThanks!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003c/aside\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImportant point for downstream analysis. DESeq2 and edgeR require unnormalized integer counts, so requesting raw matrix drops via the DepMap contact form helps prioritize future releases.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":4,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-09-19T13:16:39.786Z","reply_count":1,"reply_to_post_number":3,"quote_count":1,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":10,"readers_count":9,"score":7.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":4671,"topic_slug":"organoid-dependency-data","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":"","bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":2736,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/organoid-dependency-data/4671/4","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":7127,"name":"","username":"akacrispr","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/58956e/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-10-08T20:31:29.756Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eI also struggle to find the organoid dataset, I tried \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/pmontgom\"\u003e@pmontgom\u003c/a\u003e Density 1D, points CRISPR - however there is no option to add NextGen Model or no CRISPR+NextGen Model. will it be added soon?\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/flex035/uploads/depmap/original/2X/1/135cb87452d502c4756e57484e54a4c64c276d71.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/2LhIVVwi986LYy9KotAkQZINx1n.png?dl=1\" title=\"Screenshot 2026-10-08 at 4.31.18 PM\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/flex035/uploads/depmap/optimized/2X/1/135cb87452d502c4756e57484e54a4c64c276d71_2_355x500.png\" alt=\"Screenshot 2026-10-08 at 4.31.18 PM\" data-base62-sha1=\"2LhIVVwi986LYy9KotAkQZINx1n\" width=\"355\" height=\"500\" srcset=\"https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/flex035/uploads/depmap/optimized/2X/1/135cb87452d502c4756e57484e54a4c64c276d71_2_355x500.png, https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/flex035/uploads/depmap/optimized/2X/1/135cb87452d502c4756e57484e54a4c64c276d71_2_532x750.png 1.5x, https://canada1.discourse-cdn.com/flex035/uploads/depmap/optimized/2X/1/135cb87452d502c4756e57484e54a4c64c276d71_2_710x1000.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"E7EBF3\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eScreenshot 2026-10-08 at 4.31.18 PM\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e770×1082 47.5 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-10-08T20:31:29.756Z","reply_count":2,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":3,"reads":6,"readers_count":5,"score":26.2,"yours":false,"topic_id":4671,"topic_slug":"organoid-dependency-data","display_username":"","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":287,"hidden":false,"trust_level":1,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/organoid-dependency-data/4671/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":7138,"name":"Yejie Yun","username":"yejie_yun","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.depmap.org/yejie_yun/{size}/915_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-14T18:43:56.907Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi akacrispr,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCRISPRGeneEffect scores for organoid models can be found by filtering based on \u003ccode\u003eModel Annotation\u003c/code\u003e on Data Explorer. Under \u003ccode\u003ePrimary Annotations\u003c/code\u003e, you can identify organoid models by filtering \u003ccode\u003eGrowthPattern\u003c/code\u003e to be \u003ccode\u003eDome\u003c/code\u003e. Another option would be to use the Model.csv file under downloads which has the \u003ccode\u003eGrowthPattern\u003c/code\u003e information for each ModelID.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBest,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYejie\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":6,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-10-14T19:46:37.070Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":1.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":4671,"topic_slug":"organoid-dependency-data","display_username":"Yejie Yun","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"reply_to_user":{"id":287,"username":"akacrispr","name":"","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/58956e/{size}.png"},"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":1539,"hidden":false,"trust_level":2,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":true,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/organoid-dependency-data/4671/6","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":7139,"name":"Pmontgom","username":"pmontgom","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.depmap.org/pmontgom/{size}/4_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-14T18:59:06.208Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eJust to explain the discrepancy between what’s in the earlier messages and where you can find the data today: When the paper was released, we temporarily created a dataset in Data Explorer called “\u003ca href=\"https://depmap.org/portal/data_page/?tab=allData\u0026amp;releasename=NextGen+Model+Manuscript+2026\"\u003eNextGen Model Manuscript 2026\u003c/a\u003e” containing these new screens.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, since then we’ve released the 26Q3 data, where the organoid lines have been processed with all other CRISPR screens. Since you can now find the new models in the harmonized CRISPR dataset, we’ve removed the temporary dataset. See Yejie’s message for how to find organoid data within CRISPRGeneEffect.csv (which is the name you can find under “Downloads”. This same data is labeled “CRISPR (DepMap Public 26Q3+Score, Chronos)” in Data Explorer)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePhil\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":8,"updated_at":"2026-10-14T18:59:06.208Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":5,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":0,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":1.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":4671,"topic_slug":"organoid-dependency-data","display_username":"Pmontgom","primary_group_name":"resources-members","flair_name":"resources-members","flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group_id":47,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"